          "settings": {
            "name": "Niacinamide",
            "amount": "500 mg per labeled 2-capsule serving",
            "role": "Cellular + barrier support",
            "text": "<p>Niacinamide is a form of vitamin B3 involved in cellular energy metabolism and multiple skin-related biological processes.</p><p>Within UV Shield+, it provides a different mechanism from the formula's plant polyphenols, giving the formulation broader pathway coverage.</p>",
            "slide_set": "",
            "link_label": "Explore Niacinamide research →",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#niacinamide"
          }
        },
        "b2": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Polypodium leucotomos",
            "amount": "240 mg per labeled 2-capsule serving",
            "role": "Botanical environmental-stress support",
            "text": "<p>Polypodium leucotomos is a fern-derived botanical studied in relation to skin responses to ultraviolet exposure.</p><p>In the formula architecture, it contributes a different botanical and antioxidant profile from niacinamide and the polyphenols.</p>",
            "slide_set": "",
            "link_label": "Explore Polypodium research →",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#polypodium-leucotomos"
          }
        },
        "b3": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "EGCG",
            "amount": "200 mg per labeled 2-capsule serving",
            "role": "Polyphenol antioxidant support",
            "text": "<p>EGCG is a green-tea catechin studied for antioxidant and cell-signaling activity.</p><p>It is potentially complementary with Polypodium leucotomos and resveratrol across oxidative and inflammatory-response pathways.</p>",
            "slide_set": "",
            "link_label": "Explore EGCG research →",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#egcg"
          }
        },
        "b4": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Trans-resveratrol",
            "amount": "100 mg per labeled 2-capsule serving",
            "role": "Polyphenol cellular support",
            "text": "<p>Resveratrol is a plant polyphenol with antioxidant and cell-signaling activity.</p><p>Within the formula, it contributes overlapping but distinct redox and signaling support alongside EGCG and Polypodium leucotomos.</p>",
            "slide_set": "",
            "link_label": "Explore Resveratrol research →",
